   "evidence": "Signature at TwoInverseSets.lean:61-63 mentions only `sphere (0 : F) 1`, `E`, `IsCompact`, `Continuous`, `Injective`, `IsOpen`, `range`. Its proof uses `stereographic'`, `ContinuousLinearEquiv.ofFinrankEq` and `Homeomorph.smulOfNeZero`, with no `IsCellularSet` or `f`. The analogous chart argument in Shrink.lean:48 (`exists_continuousOn_injOn_mapsTo_sphere`) is public.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Topology/CellularSet/TwoInverseSets.lean",
   "fix": "Move it, renamed (e.g. `exists_continuous_injective_isOpen_image_ball_superset_notMem_range`), into the sphere infrastructure (e.g. `TauCeti/Topology/Sphere/Shrink.lean` next to `exists_continuousOn_injOn_mapsTo_sphere`, or a new `TauCeti/Topology/Sphere/` file), make it public and list it in that module's docstring.",
   "issue": "`exists_cell` (a compact set in S\u207f that misses `z` lies in the open cell of an embedded closed ball that also misses `z`) is stated only with Mathlib types and its proof only uses stereographic projection, nothing about cellular sets or inverse sets. Making it `private` hides reusable sphere infrastructure; the Theorem 5 assembly, which identifies closures with hemispheres, is a likely consumer.",
   "line": 61
  }
